            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Scenario:</b> An Environmental Project</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Theme:</b> How Can We Help the Environment?</p></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; border-right: none;"><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</p></td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; border-left: none;"></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td colspan="3" style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Listening: Clarify spoken instructions in collaborative tasks.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Listening: Can extract specific information from instructional videos about ways to keep the environment clean (e.g., 'Turn off the lights to save energy.').<br>Can ask for questions to clarify spoken instructions when working collaboratively (e.g., 'Put plastic in this bin.' 'Do you mean plastic bottles or all types of plastic?')<br>Can show comprehension of specific spoken instructions in environmental projects after asking for repetition (e.g., 'Can you repeat that, please?' 'Yes, put that paper in this bin.').</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

## SECTION 3 — AOA STAGES TABLE
<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher shows pictures of different places: a dirty park, a clean park, a classroom with recycling bins, and someone `plant`ing a `tree`. The teacher asks, "What do you see?" and "How can we make our `environment` clean?" Students give simple answers. The teacher introduces the theme: "Today, we will talk about how we can help the `environment`." The teacher holds up a picture of a "clean-up `project`" and explains the word `project`.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher writes "We will plant trees tomorrow" on the board. The teacher points to 'will' and models its pronunciation /wɪl/ clearly, then its contracted form 'I'll' /aɪl/. The teacher repeats, "I `will plant` trees. We `will plant` trees." The teacher then introduces imperatives by saying, "<b>Bring</b> a shovel. <b>Dig</b> a hole. <b>Water</b> the plants." The teacher uses gestures to show the meaning of `bring`, `dig`, and `water` while modeling their pronunciation.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher: "When I say, '<b>Dig</b> a hole,' do I want you to read or to make a hole in the ground?" (Expected answer: Make a hole.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Teacher: "If I say, 'We <b>will plant</b> trees,' are we `plant`ing trees now or in the `future`?" (Expected answer: In the `future`.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "An Environmental Project")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A short instructional video (1.5-2 minutes) about "How to Set Up a Classroom Recycling Station" or "Simple Steps to Keep Your School Clean." The video will feature clear, simple spoken instructions using imperatives and future simple. It will introduce vocabulary like `classroom`, `bins`, `paper`, `plastic`, `glass`, `clean`, `sort`, `recycle`.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Listening for specific instructions in a video related to environmental tasks.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>First listening (Gist):</b> The teacher plays the video once. Students listen and identify the main idea. Teacher asks: "What is the video about?" (Expected answer: How to `clean` the `classroom` / how to `recycle`.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Second listening (Specific Information):</b> The teacher provides a worksheet with 3-4 simple True/False statements or picture matching. Students listen again and mark T/F or match pictures to instructions. For example: "The video says: 'Put `plastic` in the blue bin.'" (T/F). "The video says: 'We `will clean` the `classroom` tomorrow.'" (T/F). The teacher will also prompt attention to pronunciation: "Listen for the word 'presentation'. How many parts does it have?" (pre-sen-ta-tion).</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Listening)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Listening for specific details in instructions, identifying imperatives, and recognizing future plans using 'will'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ol>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Listen and Fill:</b> The teacher plays short audio clips of instructions from the video (or similar) with a missing key word. Students listen and fill in the blank on a worksheet. (e.g., "_____ the lights to save energy." -> "Turn off"). Vocabulary includes: `clean`, `plant`, `water`, `bring`, `turn off`. This practices present simple to describe everyday events, like "We usually `wash` the plastic and `glass` bottles every day."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Sentence unscramble and Match:</b> The teacher provides scrambled sentences (e.g., "the / `plant` / `trees` / `will` / We") which students unscramble to form correct future simple statements. Then, the teacher says aloud a specific instruction (e.g., "We `will plant` `trees` next week."). Students listen and point to the correct unscrambled sentence. This also helps with pronunciation of `will` and `I'll`.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction - Listen and Clarify:</b> Students work in pairs. Teacher gives a series of simple instructions. One student is 'Listener A', the other is 'Listener B'. Listener A closes their eyes. The teacher gives an instruction to Listener B (e.g., "`Bring` the blue `paper` to the front. `Put` it on the table."). Listener B has to repeat the instruction to Listener A, and Listener A can ask for clarification: "Can you repeat that, please?" or "Do you mean the blue `paper` or the white `paper`?". This activity directly addresses the learning outcome for clarification in collaborative tasks. They then swap roles. This also integrates the pragmatic function of giving instructions and suggestions.</li>
                </ol>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "An Environmental Project")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Collaborative Planning Session with Teacher Instructions.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Students work in small groups (3-4 students). The teacher acts as the `project` leader for a "Classroom `Garden` `Project`." The teacher gives a series of multi-step verbal instructions for the `upcoming` `project`. Students must listen carefully and, collaboratively, clarify any instructions they don't understand, using phrases like "Can you repeat that, please?" or "Do you mean `plant` `flowers` or `trees`?" or "Where `will` we `dig` the hole?".</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Instructions Examples:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"For our `garden` `project`, first, `bring` small pots to `classroom` next Monday. Second, we `will dig` the soil in the `field` behind the school on Tuesday. Third, everyone `will plant` a seed. Remember, `water` the `plants` every day. Our `presentation day` is next month. We `will care` for our `plants`."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">The teacher encourages students to discuss environmental actions in group discussions, proposing ways to reduce `plastic` waste in the `classroom` if they were to `clean` it.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">The goal is for students to actively listen, follow multiple instructions, and proactively ask for clarification to ensure all group members are `ready` and `prepared` for the `project`.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h4>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Formative assessment strategy)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist during the Performance/Production stage.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students demonstrate comprehension of spoken instructions and actively ask clarifying questions during the "Classroom `Garden` `Project`" planning session.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Active Listening:</b> Students show signs of paying attention (e.g., eye contact, nodding).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Clarification Questions:</b> Students ask relevant "Can you repeat that?" or "Do you mean...?" questions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Comprehension after Clarification:</b> Students are able to restate or confirm understanding of instructions after asking for repetition.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Use of Target Vocabulary:</b> Students attempt to use new vocabulary (`plant`, `dig`, `water`, `project`, `environment`) when asking for clarification.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a quick exit ticket:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one instruction you heard today about our `project`?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Was it easy or difficult to understand all instructions? (Circle one) If difficult, why?"</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h4 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h4>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What did I learn today about how to help the `environment`?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"When I don't understand instructions, what can I say to ask for help?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What worked well in this lesson? (e.g., "Students actively asked 'Can you repeat that?'")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">What specific adjustments or scaffolds are needed for students who found clarifying instructions challenging? (e.g., "Need more pair work with sentence frames for clarification.")</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">How will this listening foundation connect to Lesson 2 (Reading Comprehension)? (e.g., "Next lesson, we `will read` a short text about a similar environmental `project` that uses many of these same vocabulary words and instructions. Students `will` need to find specific information, just like they listened for today.")</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">2-3 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>